SUPER SMASH FLASH (2006) -- SOURCE PRESERVATION
================================================

This repository holds the recovered ActionScript sources of the original
Super Smash Flash, the 2006 Flash game, together with the toolchain used
to recover them and to rebuild a single-file browser bundle.

It does NOT contain the .swf, its sprites, its sounds, or any Nintendo
material. You must supply the game file yourself. See INSTALL.

WHY
---
The game shipped only as compiled .swf. The original project files were
lost. Flash died in 2021. This is what survived, and the way back to a
runnable build.

PLAY / DOWNLOAD
---------------
The author hosts the built single-file bundle (48 MB, everything
embedded, no network needed after download):

    play:      https://newsgood.neocities.org/SuperSmash
    download:  https://newsgood.neocities.org/download
    source:    https://github.com/moon440/ssf1

The bundle itself stays out of git (it embeds third-party characters;
see docs/NOTES.md). site/download.html is the page served from the
host, kept here so the whole setup is reproducible.

WHAT IS HERE
------------
  scripts/        5,298 recovered ActionScript files, laid out by SWF
                  tag (DefineSprite_NNN/frame_N/...). This is the game
                  logic: character move tables, menus, hit detection.
  tools/          build-singlefile.mjs -- makes the one-file bundle.
  docs/NOTES.md   recovery method, fidelity report, known losses.
  KNOWN_BUGS      documented defects, causes found in the sources.
  INSTALL         how to get the game running from this repo.
  ChangeLog       history of the recovery.
  COPYING         AGPL v3. Read it.

FIDELITY
--------
AVM1 keeps identifiers in the constant pool, so names survive: what you
read here is close to what was typed in 2006. Gone forever: comments,
whitespace, the .fla timeline, layer names, and folder organisation.
Expect `var` hoisting and decompiler idiom in place of author style.
See docs/NOTES.md before complaining about a specific file.

LICENSE
